k right tackle to BUF 49 for -2 yards (30-K.Dorsey). The player down by contact was assisted by replay.","epa":0.58,"wpa":0.005,"yards":-2,"score":"34-24","role":"tackle for loss"}],"zones":{"pass":{},"recv":{},"rush":{}},"splits":{},"reports":[{"week":11,"injury":"Ankle","gameStatus":"Questionable","practice":"Limited Participation in Practice"}],"weeklyStatus":[{"week":1,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":2,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":3,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":4,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":5,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":7,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":8,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":9,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":10,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":11,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"},{"week":12,"status":"ACT","detail":"A01"}],"espn":{"summaryLabel":"2026 regular season stats","summary":[{"name":"soloTackles","label":"SOLO","value":"12","rank":"Tied-343rd"},{"name":"fumblesForced","label":"Forced Fumbles","value":"0","rank":"Tied-217th"},{"name":"interceptions","label":"Interceptions","value":"0","rank":"Tied-161st"},{"name":"passesDefended","label":"Passes Defended","value":"1","rank":"Tied-321st"}],"birthPlace":"Ontario, CA"},"news":[{"headline":"Lions 2025 free agency tracker: Offseason moves, signings","description":"Keep track of all the Lions' free agent moves throughout the 2025 offseason.","published":"2025-03-31T00:07:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/43923964/lions-2025-free-agency-tracker-offseason-moves-signings","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions' Dorsey out for year; DT McNeill, CB Davis likely done too","description":"The Lions lost three key contributors to likely season-ending injuries in CB Khalil Dorsey, DT Alim McNeill and CB Carlton Davis.","published":"2024-12-16T02:56:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/42991102/lions-dorsey-year-dt-mcneill-cb-davis-likely-done-too","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions 2024 free agency tracker: Offseason moves, signings","description":"Keep track of all the Lions' free agent moves throughout the 2024 offseason.","published":"2024-04-16T21:23:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/39533511/lions-2024-free-agency-tracker-offseason-moves-signings","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Baltimore-Pittsburgh game still on for Wednesday despite 2 more Ravens positive for COVID-19","description":"The Ravens are headed to Pittsburgh and Wednesday's game is still on, but Baltimore had two more positive COVID-19 tests before departing Tuesday, sources told ESPN's Adam Schefter.","published":"2020-12-02T06:36:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/30430540/sources-baltimore-pittsburgh-game-wednesday-2-more-ravens-positive-covid-19","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jamison Hensley","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Khalil Dorsey","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khalil_Dorsey","description":"American football player (born 1998)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:15Z","intro":"Khalil Isaiah Dorsey (born March 31, 1998) is an American professional football cornerback for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He was signed by the Baltimore Ravens as an undrafted free agent in 2020 following his college football career at Northern Arizona.","sections":[{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"BALTIMORE RAVENS\nDorsey signed with the Baltimore Ravens as an undrafted free agent following the 2020 NFL draft on May 5, 2020. He was waived during final roster cuts on September 5, and signed to the team's practice squad the next day. Dorsey was elevated to the active roster on September 28 for the team's week 3 game against the Kansas City Chiefs, and reverted to the practice squad after the game. He was elevated again on October 3 for the week 4 game against the Washington Football Team, and reverted to the practice squad again following the game. Dorsey was promoted to the active roster on October 9. He was placed on injured reserve on November 10. Dorsey was placed on the reserve/COVID-19 list by the team on November 28, and moved back to injured reserve three days later.\nOn August 16, 2021, Dorsey was placed on injured reserve.\nDuring rehabilitation for his injuries, Dorsey has won praise for his volunteer work in the community.\n\nNEW YORK GIANTS\nOn May 18, 2022, Dorsey signed with the New York Giants. He was waived by the Giants on August 30.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn December 15, 2022, Dorsey was signed to the Detroit Lions' practice squad. He signed a reserve/future contract with the team on January 9, 2023. On September 16, Dorsey was placed on injured reserve after being diagnosed with rhabdomyolysis. He was activated on October 14. In Week 17 against the Dallas Cowboys, Dorsey was part of a trick play in which he caught a 31–yard fake punt pass from Jalen Reeves-Maybin to keep the Lions' drive alive.\nOn October 27, 2024, Dorsey had a career–best 72–yard kick return in a blowout win against the Tennessee Titans. He made 14 appearances for Detroit in 2024, totaling 2 pass deflections and 14 combined tackles. On December 17, Dorsey was placed on injured reserve with an ankle injury, ending his season.\nOn March 20, 2025, Dorsey was re-signed by the Lions. On October 8, he was placed on injured reserve due to a wrist injury and a concussion. Dorsey was activated on November 22, ahead of the team's Week 12 matchup against the New York Giants."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Dorsey is of African-American and Mexican descent."}],"wikidataId":"Q100233507","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4027919","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/D/DorsKh00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/khalil-dorsey/27819","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/khalil-dorsey/9324","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khalil_Dorsey"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $1.7M is the 25th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2020 as an undrafted free agent."]}